288
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Lo yê me helke nîştî, helke. Lo yê me...
 
Hey, ours has settled well, settled. Hey ours...

289
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:33,000
Rind e, rind e? Bo loyê me çûyê le rind e?
 
Is it good, is it good? Is it good for our boy?

290
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Wê patê bagiro, têyê be kave serî te, 'erdê kave.
 
Hold that cloth, you will put it on your head, put it on the
ground.

291
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Meazez xêyî nîjî lê nanin?
 
Did Meazez put it on too?

292
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Sakın zra ve bişkênî.
 
Be careful not to break its stem.

293
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Ne bişkêne ha.
 
Don't break it, okay.

294
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

295
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:53,000
Havo boxça ye, boxçê sêvo ye, keraz ne.
 
This is a bundle, a bundle of apples, they are cherries.

296
00:20:53,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Darê sêvê li kopêş gundê Keraz ne.
 
Apple trees near the Cherry village.

297
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Berê ser vê dorê tiyê me çok so çûk dikiştan.
 
Before, on this turn, our uncle used to catch many birds.

298
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Dodo min Xoro dinîştim me, me ooy çûk dikir.
 
My uncle Xoro used to sit us down, we used to catch birds.

299
00:21:40,000 --> 00:22:00,000
Qicika me her ro li darû dana.
 
Our kids are always hitting the trees.

300
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:03,000
Meazez çoyê mero çêdike.
 
Meazez is making tea for us.

301
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:11,000
A rastî Meazez... tabaan me kozus xwar û nuyî, kozus şêrîn
e... no teva xwarin.
 
Actually Meazez... of course we ate fresh walnuts, sweet
walnuts... don't eat them all.

302
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:16,000
Vê çoyê mero çêke, çay û qehwa kowa me çêkin.
 
Make this tea for us, make all our tea and coffee.

303
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:35,000
Çayê ser êr jî pir xweş e.
 
Tea over the fire is also very good.

304
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:41,000
Walla cewkî pir xweş e. Havolno. Cewkî xweş xweş.
 
By God, the weather is very good. Friends. A very good
atmosphere.

305
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:44,000
Xayê mero bin vê dorê tê.
 
Our family comes under this tree.

306
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:50,000
Hesê çûka, hesê... boki pak... ano xayê mero tê l'vê deştê.
 
Sound of birds, sound of... clean wind... our family comes
to this plain.

307
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:53,000
Cew cî hêdî, hesela ye, xelqê mero ano fera dibe.
 
The weather is calm, it's peaceful, our people here get
relief.

308
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:55,000
Cew cî pir xweş e.
 
The weather is very good.

309
00:22:55,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Em kê nuka çay û qehwê jî vexwin.
 
We will now drink tea and coffee too.

310
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Law rûnên hûn ê benî hencê xwedê bin. Ev bera necihê helkê.
 
Hey sit down, you will be under God's grace. This stone is
not a place for jumping.

311
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:25,000
Aha, ew sa t'evek daxînim.
 
Aha, I will drop that bunch.

312
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Çayê ser tarofê çok so... bînî xo xweş e.
 
Tea on the stand is very... its smell is good.

313
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:38,000
Warem hesûbî we jî kirîye ho, nîvanê me ne. Warem çayekê
vexwin.
 
Come, we have accounted for you too, you are our guests.
Come drink a tea.

314
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:41,000
Çayek ano ser êr û l'bin vê sersiyê...
 
A tea here on the fire and under this shade...

315
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:49,000
Cewkî romensî ye.
 
A romantic atmosphere.

316
00:23:49,000 --> 00:24:09,000
Valla ez 'alena Meazez. En Meazez jî û Semîr jî.
 
By God I am with Meazez. Both Meazez and Semir.

317
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:12,000
Selat û 'enebî...
 
Blessings on the Prophet...

318
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:17,000
Maşalla, ehar derim derekê... ano nuzum.
 
Mashallah, everywhere I go to a place... I don't know.

319
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:25,000
Maşalla selat û 'enebî...
 
Mashallah, blessings on the Prophet...

320
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:45,000
Mero aşiqê caka dibe.
 
One falls in love with the place.

321
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:13,000
Erê hevalno, tab'an vê derê emî vêrdiben Kitxe.
 
Yes friends, of course we call this place Kitxe.

322
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:15,000
Kitxe emî mala xalê Elî ne.
 
Kitxe, we are at Uncle Ali's house.

323
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:19,000
Bi leqeb vêra dibên Elî Lastîk.
 
By nickname they call him Ali Lastik (Rubber).

324
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:21,000
We ne bîn kes nusnokin... bas malê xalê Elî ye.
 
Don't be people who... but it is Uncle Ali's house.

325
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:28,000
Ev kilfet ne, li vê derê ne, maşalla cuxrafiyek ginde,
mentiqek ginde, tebî'etek ginde pir xweş e.
 
These are the family, they are here, mashallah a village
geography, a village area, a village nature that is very
nice.

326
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Em drêker b'çûn me go em jamrin silavêkî pê dinê.
 
We were on the way going, we said let's stop by and give a
greeting.

327
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:36,000
Yanî pir cewkî xweş e û ano seke xizmet milkê xo dikin,
ıxlas.
 
Meaning a very nice atmosphere and look how they serve their
property, sincerely.

328
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:38,000
Hemol momol o nînin.
 
There are no porters or workers.

329
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:43,000
Maşalla milletê me yê Kurmanc, pêşketî ye, feqet dom cem
heye.
 
Mashallah our Kurmanji people are advanced, only if there is
unity.

330
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Xalê Elî... ti dibê çi? Kasekî dima seyr dike, dûr û welat.
 
Uncle Ali... what do you say? Someone watching us, far away
and in the country.

331
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:53,000
Lo ehlen we sehlen cîrantî ro, cema'etî ro, sa'eta we xweş.
 
Oh welcome to the neighborhood, to the community, good
health to you.

332
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Ser çavê me, ser çava.
 
Upon our eyes, upon eyes (You're welcome).

333
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:57,000
Xwedê rehetîyê bide we, de ehlen serê me û çavê me.
 
May God give you comfort, welcome upon our head and our
eyes.

334
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Silavê te heye bigihînim?
 
Do you have a greeting I should convey?

335
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:01,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

336
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:03,000
Kasekî li me seyr dike silavê teybet ji gihînim.
 
Anyone watching us, I convey special greetings.

337
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:05,000
Destê me jî ji Giyara ne.
 
Our origin is also from Giyara.

338
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:10,000
Ehlen we sehlen cîrantî Giyara, batnê wa... û silavê me ji
bira da hene.
 
Welcome to the Giyara neighborhood, their womb... and our
greetings are there from the heart.

339
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:13,000
Heta paşiya dinê ji kurmên cê me ji Giyara ne...
 
Until the end of the world, our Kurds are from Giyara...

340
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:18,000
...ji evojîra, no roj eraba, no roj kurmanca... ji Giyara
ne.
 
...from there, not Arabs, not Kurds... they are from Giyara.

341
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:20,000
Tev xweş xelkî.
 
All good people.

342
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:25,000
Wî li me seyr dike jî sa'eta giya xweş û dilî kê tê ray
bîrin wancame.
 
Whoever watches us too, good health to all, and may the
heart...

343
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Sa'eta te xweş, xwedê 'emrekî dirêj bide te.
 
Good health to you, may God give you a long life.

344
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Xaltîk bereket, 'emr çend e?
 
Auntie Blessing, how old are you?

345
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Wallahî nizanim... 'Elî... wele temê xwedê zane çend e.
 
By God I don't know... Ali... by God only God knows the
amount.

346
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Heftê heye?
 
Is it seventy?

347
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Heftê, heftê çend e kuro?
 
Seventy, seventy what son?

348
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:41,000
Maşalla, maşalla, xwedê 'emrekî dirêj bide.
 
Mashallah, may God give a long life.

349
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Ele xolî min.
 
Oh my dear.

350
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:43,000
Ez ji heftêya mezin im.
 
I am older than seventy.

351
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Maşalla, xwedê 'emrekî dirêj bide te.
 
Mashallah, may God give you a long life.

352
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:48,000
Qicik hene bereket? Çend ne?
 
Are there children, blessing? How many?

353
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:50,000
Deh donzdeh hene.
 
There are ten, twelve.

354
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Xwedê ji te ra bihêle, xwedê destê wa ser gora bigire.
 
May God keep them for you, may God hold their hands.

355
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:58,000
Sağol lo, çera bî de bes ka cema'eta ne em bi tenê ne li vî
gundî.
 
Thanks, may you be a light, but where is the community, we
are alone in this village.

356
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Qede ye, qede ye. Lo de mereke beçe şta heyat wabi westa.
 
It's destiny. Don't worry, life is like this now.

357
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:05,000
Êcê me yek li gund e, yek li Heleb e, lawkê me yê li Heleb
e, hebe ji êl zotil derbana.
 
Our kids, one is in the village, one is in Aleppo, our boy
in Aleppo...

358
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:08,000
Silavê me ji wan ji Giyara ne.
 
Our greetings to them are from Giyara.

359
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:16,000
Silavê teybet ji gihînine û elî te jî seyr kin, qicikê weyî
li we seyr kin inşalla bi izna xwedê.
 
We convey special greetings and they will watch you, your
little ones will watch you, God willing, with God's
permission.

360
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:20,000
Erê hevalno, taba'an em gihîştin dawiya vîdeoya xo.
 
Yes friends, of course we reached the end of our video.

361
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:24,000
Sa'eta her kesî kî li me seyr dike xweş, çavê weyê gimoş
dikim.
 
Good health to everyone who watches us, I kiss your
beautiful eyes.

362
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:29,000
Em jam xalê Elî rûniştin, xwedê pêxember ji ê razî be û
xwedê 'emrekî dirêj bide.
 
We sat with Uncle Ali, may God and the Prophet be pleased
with him and may God give him a long life.

363
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:34,000
Insanekî kibar e, insanekî mezin e, tora xo ge dîrok...
 
A noble human, a great human, his tradition is history...

364
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:38,000
Ez pir de ra digerim, însanê mezin gelek xêr û bereket e.
 
I travel around a lot, great people are much goodness and
blessing.

365
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:44,000
Û di mala xo da jî, wexta awê ezmê ser me çêbî, ji mala xo
jî derneket.
 
And in his house too, when that trouble happened over us, he
didn't leave his house.

366
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Berxwedan bî ji xolî mero serkeftin be, her bijî ez dibêm
her bijî.
 
It was resistance, from our soil may there be victory, long
live I say long live.

367
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Vîdyokî demxweş hacer bimênin inşalla helqek dinemê.
 
Remain in a good-time video... God willing in another
episode.

368
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Xwedê ji we jî razî be, xwedê 'emrekî dirêj bide we.
 
May God be pleased with you too, may God give you a long
life.

369
00:28:54,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Sa'eta we jî rehet bibe û li me seyr ke û xwedê rehetîkê
bide nexweşê her mala xwedê.
 
May your time be comfortable too and watch us and may God
give comfort to the sick of every house of God.

370
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Silav û hurmet.
 
Greetings and respect.

371
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:25,000
Merheba.
 
Hello.

372
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

373
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:35,000
Keremke, keremke.
 
Please, come in.

374
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:40,000
Ser çava.
 
You're welcome (upon eyes).

375
00:29:40,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Em b'xêr hatin.
 
Welcome to us.

376
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:10,000
Kurê min, ew jî li xerîbiyê ye.
 
My son, he is also abroad.

377
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:13,000
Heta em sax bin...
 
As long as we are alive...

378
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:16,000
Xwedê emrê we dirêj ke.
 
May God prolong your life.

379
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:20,000
Heta em sax bin, em ê vana xwedî kin.
 
As long as we are alive, we will take care of them.

380
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Em nikarin... yanî dilê me bernade.
 
We cannot... meaning our hearts do not allow it.

381
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:31,000
We ev der kiriye mîna bihuştê.
 
You have made this place like paradise.

